{{Quote|According to some, the starbird can never die&mdash;whenever it seems to be gone, it's actually renewing itself in the heart of a nova.|From Sabine Wren's personal journal|<ref name="sketch" />}}
The '''starbird''',<ref name="sketch" /> also known as a '''phoenix''',<ref name="Aftermath">[[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']]</ref> was a legendary [[Bird|avian]] creature that was thought to be [[Immortality|immortal]]. Allegedly, when it seemed to be [[Death|dead]], the starbird was actually renewing itself in the heart of a [[nova]]. [[Sabine Wren]], a member of the [[Spectres]], used a [[Starbird (symbol)|stylized starbird]] as her personal signature.<ref name="sketch" /> Later, the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]],<ref name="Ultimate">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> the [[New Republic]], and the [[Resistance]] also used stylized starbirds in their [[Rebel Alliance starbird|respective]] [[Sigil of the New Republic|insignias]].<ref name="Visual">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

In some naturalistic sketches she drew for [[Sabine Wren's journal|her personal journal]], Sabine Wren depicted the starbird as having two wings, a moderately long tail, and a crest of feathers on its head.<ref name="sketch" />

